## 2. What I missed (delta vs. prior audit)

The prior audit (win_c_emit_compat.oot) walked 4-5 c_emit files in depth (preamble, meta, verify, sys) and grep'd the rest for the canonical extensions. The deep re-walk surfaces these items that grep alone missed:

| Delta | What | File:line | Reason | Risk under mingw |
|-------|------|-----------|--------|------------------|
| GCC `({...})` statement expression | c_try_unwrap emits `({ OoResS __q = call; ... })` | c_emit_result.oo:180 | grep for `({...})` returns 0 because the literal starts mid-string. Direct read finds it. | mingw-w64 gcc supports. MSVC cl does not. Phase 1 = mingw: OK. |
| C99 compound-literal of array (2nd site) | sys_exec builds `(OoStr[]){...}` for user argv | c_emit_lower.oo:166-167 | prior audit only cited c_emit_sys.oo:165. The 2nd site uses user argv (no `sh` literal). | C99 standard. mingw supports. OK. |
| C99 compound-literal of struct (many sites) | Ok/Err ctor, sum ctor, Result return, OoResV mapping | c_emit_result.oo:64, 67, 70, 73, 76, 79, 82, 85, 89, 93, 96, 99, 101, 105, 108, 111, 114, 117, 120, 123, 126, 130, 133; c_emit_sum.oo:111, 114, 120; c_emit_arc_2.oo:57 | grep for `\{\s*\.` returned 0 hits. Read finds them. | C99 standard. mingw supports. OK. |
| C99 designated initializers | `((Name){.f1 = v1, .f2 = v2})` in struct lit | c_emit_lower.oo:90 | regex needed a space. Read finds it. | C99 standard. mingw supports. OK. |
| `volatile` keyword in decoys | 4 sites in c_emit_meta.oo | c_emit_meta.oo:137, 140, 144, 148 | prior audit cited `__attribute__` but not the body lines. | C standard. Portable. OK. |
| Plain `fprintf`, `exit(1)` in generated C | 30+ sites, every error path | c_emit_preamble.oo:159-174, c_emit_result.oo:180, c_emit_olist.oo:48, 51, c_emit_verify.oo:43, etc. | prior audit cited preamble only. | Standard C. mingw supports. OK. |
| `malloc` / `memcpy` / `size_t` | runtime alloc in OoL_ push | c_emit_olist.oo:56, 58 | prior audit cited preamble headers; not the emit body. | Standard C. mingw supports. OK. |
| `unsigned int __oo_meta_pad` and `unsigned char __oo_meta_buf[16]` | layout decoys | c_emit_meta.oo:137, 140, 144, 148 | prior audit cited attribute; not the body. | Standard C. Portable. OK. |
| `#ifndef OO_TY_<name>` / `#ifndef OO_FWD_<name>` / `#ifndef OO_HAVE_<name>` / `#ifndef OO_FNS_<name>` | include-guard duplication | c_emit_struct.oo:121, 126; c_emit_olist.oo:13, 16, 21, 24, 43, 60 | prior audit cited oo_meta `__GNUC__` only. | Standard C preprocessor. OK. |

The other half of the source -- secret guards, libfloor/netio/sys calls, ops, match, ident, let, fn, arc, struct, sum, list, walk, result, contract, env, helpers, args, temps, call, call_ty, secret, secret_alias, secret_check, secret_guard, secret_prop, secret_prop_scan, skip, skip_grant, skip_peek, sum_spec, ty, ty_ext, lower, match_let, match_stmt, list_ty, let_ext, let_ext_crt, deref, stmt, for, fn, print, max_cycles, walk, olist, ops_str, ops, arc_2, struct, sum, sum_spec, result_ty, result, env, contract, call_ty, call, args, helpers, deref -- **adds zero** non-portable constructs. Everything is plain C99 + the two extensions already known (`__attribute__` and `({...})`).

